# Path normalization

Two path levels — never mix them. Full spec: `.cursor/interface/paths.md`.

## Relative (API, UI, VCS)

- Always **forward slashes**: `assets/scene.blend`, `.DFM/tmp_review`
- Normalize on input: `filepath.ToSlash`, trim `./`, trim leading/trailing `/`
- Go: `utils.NormalizeRepoRelPath` / `canonicalRelPath` in jsonapi
- Join to filesystem: `filepath.Join(repoRoot, filepath.FromSlash(rel))` or `utils.JoinRepoPath`

## Absolute (filesystem, cfg, OS open)

- **Native OS separators**: `/` on Unix, `\` on Windows
- Normalize before store/compare: `filepath.Abs` + `filepath.Clean`
- Before `open` / `xdg-open` / `ShellExecute`: `filepath.EvalSymlinks` on the native abs path

## Rules

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Accept `\` in API input, normalize to `/` for relative (`ReplaceAll` — not only `ToSlash`) | Store relative paths with `\` in JSON/UI |
| Use `FromSlash(rel)` before `filepath.Dir` / `Join` | Call `filepath.Dir` on slash-only paths without `FromSlash` |
| Return native abs from FS operations (toast, cfg) | Return mixed `C:/foo\bar` without cleaning |
| Compare abs paths case-insensitively on Windows | Compare raw strings across platforms |

## Compare / tmp_review

- API path: `.DFM/tmp_review` (relative, `/`)
- FS path: `filepath.Join(repoPath, ".DFM", "tmp_review")` (native abs)
- Only `workdir.open` may access `.DFM/tmp_review`; other workdir endpoints still hide `.DFM/`
